<body>
    <table
        style="width:100%;max-width:800px;border:0px;border-spacing:0px;border-collapse:separate;margin-right:auto;margin-left:auto;">
        <tbody>
            <tr style="padding:0px">
                <td style="padding:0px">
                    <table
                        style="width:100%;border:0px;border-spacing:0px;border-collapse:separate;margin-right:auto;margin-left:auto;">
                        <tbody>
                            <tr style="padding:0px">
                                <td style="padding:2.5%;width:63%;vertical-align:middle">
                                    <p style="text-align:center">
                                        <name>Gautam Sreekumar</name>
                                    </p>
                                    <p>I am a Ph.D. candidate supervised by <a href="https://vishnu.boddeti.net/">Dr.
                                            Vishnu Naresh Boddeti</a>
                                        at <a href="https://msu.edu/">Michigan State
                                            University</a>. Previously, I have worked at
                                        <a href="https://www.qualcomm.com/company/locations/india">Qualcomm India</a> as
                                        a software engineer. I obtained my B.Tech. in
                                        Electrical Engineering from
                                        <a href="https://www.iitm.ac.in/">Indian Institute of
                                            Technology Madras</a> where my undergraduate thesis was
                                        advised by <a href="https://www.ee.iitm.ac.in/raju/">Dr. A.N. Rajagopalan</a>.
                                    </p>
                                    <p>
                                        My research focuses on building
                                        safe and robust machine learning
                                        models. Some of the
                                        applications include <a
                                        href="https://arxiv.org/abs/2507.05412">improving robustness
                                        against distributional shifts</a>,
                                        <a href="https://arxiv.org/abs/2509.12263">evaluating inductive physical
                                        reasoning in LLMs</a>,
                                        <a href="https://arxiv.org/abs/2503.01145">improving the
                                        controllability of diffusion
                                        models for compositional generation</a>, and
                                        <a
                                        href="https://arxiv.org/abs/2501.00962">evaluating
                                        stereotypes in T2I models</a>.
                                    </p>
                                    <p style="text-align:center">
                                        <a href="mailto:sreekum1@msu.edu">Email</a> &nbsp/&nbsp
                                        <a
                                            href="https://scholar.google.com/citations?hl=en&user=mBrW_AkAAAAJ&view_op=list_works&sortby=pubdate">Google
                                            Scholar</a> &nbsp/&nbsp
                                        <a href="https://x.com/gautamsree_">X</a> &nbsp/&nbsp
                                        <a href="https://github.com/gautamsreekumar">Github</a>
                                    </p>
                                </td>
                                <td style="padding:2.5%;width:40%;max-width:40%">
                                    <a href="images/gautamsreekumar.jpg"><img style="width:100%;max-width:100%"
                                            alt="profile photo" src="images/gautamsreekumar_circle.png"
                                            class="hoverZoomLink"></a>
                                </td>
                            </tr>
                        </tbody>
                    </table>
                    
                    <table
                        style="width:100%;border:0px;border-spacing:0px;border-collapse:separate;margin-right:auto;margin-left:auto;">
                        <tbody>
                            <tr>
                                <td style="padding:10px;width:100%;vertical-align:middle;text-align:center">
                                    <p style="color:purple;margin:0">I
                                    am looking for full-time research
                                    scientist/engineer positions.</p>
                                </td>
                            </tr>
                            <tr>
                                <td style="padding:20px;width:100%;vertical-align:middle">
                                    <heading>Research</heading>
                                </td>
                            </tr>
                            <tr>
                                <td>
                                    Click on the image thumbnails to view the full-size
                                    image in a new tab.
                                </td>
                            </tr>
                        </tbody>
                    </table>
                    <table
                        style="width:100%;border:0px;border-spacing:0px;border-collapse:separate;margin-right:auto;margin-left:auto;">
                        <tbody>

                            <tr>
                                <td style="padding:20px;width:25%;vertical-align:middle" align="center">
                                    <img src='images/inphyre.png' width="180"
                                        onclick="window.open('images/inphyre.png', '_blank');">
                                </td>
                                <td style="padding:20px;width:75%;vertical-align:middle">
                                    <papertitle>InPhyRe Discovers: Large Multimodal Models
                                        Struggle in Inductive Physical Reasoning</papertitle>
                                    <br>
                                    <strong>Gautam Sreekumar</strong>,
                                    <a href="https://vishnu.boddeti.net/">Vishnu Naresh
                                        Boddeti</a>
                                    <br>
                                    <em>TMLR</em>, 2026
                                    <br>
                                    <a
                                    href="https://arxiv.org/abs/2509.12263">arXiv</a>
                                    | <a
                                    href="https://gautamsreekumar.github.io/project_pages/inphyre/index.html">Project
                                    page</a> | <a
                                    href="https://x.com/gautamsree_/status/2061502274841489544">X
                                    Thread</a>
                                    <p></p>
                                    <p>
                                        Our physical reasoning
                                        benchmark, InPhyRe, reveals that
                                        large multimodal models struggle
                                        to infer the underlying physical
                                        laws and apply them for physical
                                        reasoning when these underlying
                                        physical laws differ from what
                                        were seen during the models'
                                        training.
                                    </p>
                                </td>
                            </tr>
                            <tr>
                                <td style="padding:20px;width:25%;vertical-align:middle" align="center">
                                    <img src='images/replin.png' width="180"
                                        onclick="window.open('images/replin.png', '_blank');">
                                </td>
                                <td style="padding:20px;width:75%;vertical-align:middle">
                                    <papertitle>Incorporating Interventional Independence Improves Robustness against
                                        Interventional Distribution Shift</papertitle>
                                    <br>
                                    <strong>Gautam Sreekumar</strong>,
                                    <a href="https://vishnu.boddeti.net/">Vishnu Naresh
                                        Boddeti</a>
                                    <br>
                                    <em>TMLR</em>, 2025
                                    <br>
                                    <a
                                    href="https://arxiv.org/abs/2507.05412">arXiv</a> | <a href="https://gautamsreekumar.github.io/project_pages/replin/index.html">Project page</a>
                                    <p></p>
                                    <p>
                                        Explicitly enforcing statistical independence between
                                        the representations of an intervened nodes and its
                                        non-descendants improves the robustness of learned
                                        representations towards interventional distribution
                                        shifts.
                                    </p>
                                </td>
                            </tr>

                            <tr>
                                <td style="padding:20px;width:25%;vertical-align:middle" align="center">
                                    <img src='images/CoInD.png' width="180"
                                        onclick="window.open('images/CoInD.png', '_blank');">
                                </td>
                                <td style="padding:20px;width:75%;vertical-align:middle">
                                    <papertitle>CoInD: Enabling Logical Compositions in
                                        Diffusion Models</papertitle>
                                    <br>
                                    <a href="https://sachit3022.github.io/">Sachit Gaudi</a>,
                                    <strong>Gautam Sreekumar</strong>,
                                    <a href="https://vishnu.boddeti.net/">Vishnu Naresh
                                        Boddeti</a>
                                    <br>
                                    <em>ICLR</em>, 2025
                                    <br>
                                    <a href="https://arxiv.org/abs/2503.01145">arXiv</a>
                                    <p></p>
                                    <p>
                                        Enforcing conditional independence between the
                                        attributes significantly improves logical compositionality in
                                        diffusion models, especially when the demanded compositions
                                        are not observed during training.
                                    </p>
                                </td>
                            </tr>

                            <tr>
                                <td style="padding:20px;width:25%;vertical-align:middle" align="center">
                                    <img src='images/OASIS.png' width="180"
                                        onclick="window.open('images/OASIS.png', '_blank');">
                                </td>
                                <td style="padding:20px;width:75%;vertical-align:middle">
                                    <papertitle>OASIS Uncovers: High-Quality T2I Models,
                                        Same Old Stereotypes</papertitle>
                                    <br>
                                    <a href="https://sepehrdehdashtian.github.io/">Sepehr Dehdashtian</a>,
                                    <strong>Gautam Sreekumar</strong>,
                                    <a href="https://vishnu.boddeti.net/">Vishnu Naresh
                                        Boddeti</a>
                                    <br>
                                    <em>ICLR</em>, 2025 <span
                                        style="font-weight: bold; color: #9F2B68">(Spotlight)</span>
                                    <br>
                                    <a href="https://arxiv.org/abs/2501.00962">arXiv</a> | <a href="https://sepehrdehdashtian.github.io/Papers/OASIS/index.html">Project page</a>
                                    <p></p>
                                    <p>
                                        The high-fidelity images generated by T2I models such
                                        as FLUX and SD3 still exhibit stereotypes about gender
                                        and nationalities.
                                    </p>
                                </td>
                            </tr>

                            <tr>
                                <td style="padding:20px;width:25%;vertical-align:middle" align="center">
                                    <!-- <div class="one"> -->
                                    <img src='images/PINN-Stress.png' height="120"
                                        onclick="window.open('images/PINN-Stress.png', '_blank');">
                                    <!-- </div> -->
                                </td>
                                <td style="padding:20px;width:75%;vertical-align:middle">
                                    <papertitle>Physics Informed Neural Network for
                                        Dynamic Stress Prediction</papertitle>
                                    <br>
                                    <a href="https://bolandih.github.io/">Hamed Bolandi</a>,
                                    <strong>Gautam Sreekumar</strong>,
                                    <a href="https://hal.cse.msu.edu/team/xuyang-li/">Xuyang Li</a>,
                                    <a href="https://www.egr.msu.edu/~lajnefni/">Nizar Lajnef</a>, <br>
                                    <a href="https://vishnu.boddeti.net/">Vishnu Naresh
                                        Boddeti</a>
                                    <br>
                                    <em>Applied Intelligence</em>, 2023
                                    <br>
                                    <a href="https://arxiv.org/abs/2211.16190">arXiv</a>
                                    <p></p>
                                    <p>
                                        Enforcing PDE constraints in a model to predict
                                        dynamic stress distribution from a sequence of sensor
                                        readings of the load on a Gusset plate.
                                    </p>
                                </td>
                            </tr>

                            <tr>
                                <td style="width:25%;vertical-align:middle;border:0px" align="center">
                                    <img src='images/face-capacity.png' width="180"
                                        onclick="window.open('images/face-capacity.png', '_blank');">
                                </td>
                                <td style="padding:20px;width:75%;vertical-align:middle;border:0px">
                                    <papertitle>On the Biometric Capacity of Generative Face Models</papertitle>
                                    <br>
                                    <a href="https://vishnu.boddeti.net/">Vishnu Naresh Boddeti</a>,
                                    <strong>Gautam Sreekumar</strong>,
                                    <a href="https://cse.msu.edu/~rossarun/">Arun Ross</a>,
                                    <br>
                                    <em>IJCB</em>, 2023
                                    <br>
                                    <a href="https://arxiv.org/abs/2308.02065">arXiv</a>
                                    <p></p>
                                    <p>
                                        Estimating an upper bound on the capacity of
                                        generative models to create unique identities using
                                        face feature extractors.
                                    </p>
                                </td>
                            </tr>

                            <tr>
                                <td style="width:25%;vertical-align:middle;border:0px" align="center">
                                    <img src='images/Spurious-Correlations.png' width="180"
                                        onclick="window.open('images/Spurious-Correlations.png', '_blank');">
                                </td>
                                <td style="padding:20px;width:75%;vertical-align:middle;border:0px">
                                    <papertitle>Spurious Correlations and Where to Find Them</papertitle>
                                    <br>
                                    <strong>Gautam Sreekumar</strong>,
                                    <a href="https://vishnu.boddeti.net/">Vishnu Naresh Boddeti</a>,
                                    <br>
                                    <em>2nd SCIS Workshop at ICML</em>, 2023
                                    <br>
                                    <a href="https://arxiv.org/abs/2308.11043">arXiv</a>
                                    <p></p>
                                    <p>
                                        Jointly analyzing commonly studied causes of
                                        spurious correlations in ERM models to aid the
                                        design of spurious correlation mitigation techniques.
                                    </p>
                                </td>
                            </tr>

                            <tr>
                                <td style="padding:20px;width:25%;vertical-align:middle" align="center">
                                    <img src='images/HADAR.png' width="180"
                                        onclick="window.open('images/HADAR.png', '_blank');">
                                </td>
                                <td style="padding:20px;width:75%;vertical-align:middle">
                                    <papertitle>Heat-assisted Detection and Ranging</papertitle>
                                    <br>
                                    <a href="https://electrodynamics.org/people/dr-fanglin-bao">Fanglin Bao</a>,
                                    <a href="https://electrodynamics.org/people/xueji-wang">Xueji
                                        Wang</a>,
                                    <a href="https://shreehari117.github.io/">Shree
                                        Hari Sureshbabu</a>,
                                    <strong>Gautam Sreekumar</strong>,
                                    <a href="https://scholar.google.com/citations?user=pFf9znsAAAAJ&hl=en">Liping
                                        Yang</a>,
                                    <a href="https://web.ics.purdue.edu/~vaneet/">Vaneet Aggarwal</a>,
                                    <a href="https://vishnu.boddeti.net/">Vishnu Naresh Boddeti</a>,
                                    <a href="http://www.electrodynamics.org/">Zubin Jacob</a>
                                    <br>
                                    <em>Nature</em>, 2023 <span style="font-weight: bold; color:
                  #9F2B68">(Cover article)</span>
                                    <br>
                                    <a href="https://www.nature.com/articles/s41586-023-06174-6">Paper</a>
                                    &nbsp/&nbsp <a href="https://www.nature.com/articles/d41586-023-02333-x">Cover
                                        article</a>
                                    &nbsp/&nbsp <a href="https://www.nature.com/nature/volumes/619/issues/7971">Cover
                                        image</a>
                                    <p></p>
                                    <strong>Press Coverage:</strong> <a
                                        href="https://www.science.org/content/article/ai-brings-clarity-fuzzy-night-vision-images">
                                        Science</a>, <a
                                        href="https://techxplore.com/news/2023-07-ghost-busting-heat-assisted-ranging-clarity-thermal.html">
                                        Tech Xplore</a>, <a
                                        href="https://www.popsci.com/technology/hadar-thermal-camera/">Popular
                                        Science</a>, <a
                                        href="https://www.theregister.com/2023/07/27/hadar_night_vision_av/">The
                                        Register</a>, <a
                                        href="https://www.newscientist.com/article/2384435-driverless-cars-could-get-ai-powered-heat-vision-for-nighttime-driving/">New
                                        Scientist</a>, <a
                                        href="https://www.maginative.com/article/seeing-through-darkness/">Maginative</a>,
                                    <a
                                        href="https://phys.org/news/2023-08-thermal-imaging-ai-pitch-darkness.html">Phys.org</a>
                                    <p>
                                        Enabling machine learning models to see in the dark
                                        by decomposing passive heat signals into
                                        temperature, emissivity and texture.
                                    </p>
                                </td>
                            </tr>

                            <tr>
                                <td style="padding:20px;width:25%;vertical-align:middle" align="center">
                                    <img src='images/Neuro-DynaStress.png' width="180"
                                        onclick="window.open('images/Neuro-DynaStress.png', '_blank');">
                                </td>
                                <td style="padding:20px;width:75%;vertical-align:middle">
                                    <papertitle>Neuro-DynaStress: Preedicting Dynamic
                                        Stress Distributions in Structural Components</papertitle>
                                    <br>
                                    <a href="https://bolandih.github.io/">Hamed Bolandi</a>,
                                    <strong>Gautam Sreekumar</strong>,
                                    <a href="https://hal.cse.msu.edu/team/xuyang-li/">Xuyang Li</a>,
                                    <a href="https://www.egr.msu.edu/~lajnefni/">Nizar Lajnef</a>, <br>
                                    <a href="https://vishnu.boddeti.net/">Vishnu Naresh
                                        Boddeti</a>
                                    <br>
                                    <em>ArXiv</em>, 2023
                                    <br>
                                    <a href="https://arxiv.org/abs/2301.02580">arXiv</a>
                                    <p></p>
                                    <p>
                                        Predicting dynamic stress distribution from load sequence,
                                        geometry and boundary conditions using
                                        image-to-image models.
                                    </p>
                                </td>
                            </tr>

                            <tr>
                                <td style="padding:20px;width:25%;vertical-align:middle" align="center">
                                    <img src='images/NAT.png' height="120"
                                        onclick="window.open('images/NAT.png', '_blank');">
                                </td>
                                <td style="padding:20px;width:75%;vertical-align:middle">
                                    <papertitle>Neural Architecture Transfer</papertitle>
                                    <br>
                                    <a href="https://www.zhichaolu.com/">Zhichao Lu</a>,
                                    <strong>Gautam Sreekumar</strong>,
                                    <a href="https://www.egr.msu.edu/~goodman/">Erik Goodman</a>,
                                    <a href="https://www.cse.msu.edu/~banzhafw/">Wolfgang Banzhaf</a>, <br>
                                    <a href="https://www.egr.msu.edu/~kdeb/">Kalyanmoy Deb</a>,
                                    <a href="https://vishnu.boddeti.net/">Vishnu Naresh
                                        Boddeti</a>
                                    <br>
                                    <em>T-PAMI</em>, 2021
                                    <br>
                                    <a href="https://arxiv.org/abs/2005.05859">arXiv</a>
                                    <p></p>
                                    <p>
                                        We provide an evolutionary algorithm to search pareto-optimal architectures
                                        from a supernet trained on ImageNet.
                                    </p>
                                </td>
                            </tr>

